    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0455" n="1209" xml:id="pg1209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/106</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-08T12:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1917, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 9.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>819. Department’s 697, October 5, 5 p.m., concerning British-Spanish agreement
                    fuel and iron ore. British Ambassador handed me today memorandum in which
                    appears following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The British Government understands that unless supplies reach Spain
                            shortly, the position of the present Government, which is friendly, may
                            be seriously affected, owing to the urgent need of coal.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
